************ Monolithic VS Micro-Service Architecture ****************************

1.Monolithic Architecture

it has a single unit for storing entire program

ef we have an e commerce website so 

-shopping UI
-Payment gateway
-checkout page
-order page
-cart
-discount service
.....

it has a single codebase

Users -> LB -> App -> Db

So for simple sites


2.Mircoservice arch:

It divides application into different components

                    - Shop UI            - DB, Messaging queue
User -> API Gateway - Payment gateway    - DB
                    - Order service      -DB


************ Horizontal & Vertical Scaling ****************************

Lets say that when we build our app we procured 1TB of database, now after few years the db is almost full ok now i need more space to handle the load so there are 2 ways to do this
Horizontal nad vertical scaling.

1.Vertical scaling :

Increasing the capacity or capability of any hardware or software component is called vertical scaling.

so if we increase from 1TB -> 2TB its vertical scaling

Major problem or limitation :
that lets say we can scale upto 10 TB nd cannot go beyond this.


Now, if we somehow want to go beyond the 10 TB, then we have to take help of horizontal scaling
-also known as scaling out
DB1 + DB2 + DB3 we cann add more db's
We also get 'Fault Tolerance' , eg in future 1 db gets down but we have other db's like db2 and db3 traffic can be diverted.

cons: its complex and not easy to handle


Now, when to use which scaling:

Factors:
-Performance requirement (if we want system to be up all the time)
-Avalability requirement
-Scalability Goal
